Add the NativeDwc3 built-in personality. Like NativeUfs's root personality, it
matches the platform-expert (root) device so the probe can start early, before the
original AMFI. It is unconditional: a personality is a runtime string resolved by
class name, so when the NativeDwc3 archive is not linked (any board that does not
force_load libNativeDwc3.a) IOKit simply finds no such class and does not match.
On fajita the archive is linked (CONFIG_XNU_EXTRA_LD_ARCHIVES); the driver is still
default-off, doing nothing unless the boot argument native-dwc3-probe=1 is set.
Applies after native-aes-personality.patch, which adds the NativeUfs block above.
diff --git a/iokit/KernelConfigTables.cpp b/iokit/KernelConfigTables.cpp
--- a/iokit/KernelConfigTables.cpp
+++ b/iokit/KernelConfigTables.cpp
@@ -105,4 +105,10 @@
     "     'IOProbeScore'    = 500:32;"
     "   }"
 #endif
+    "   ,{"
+    "     'IOClass'         = NativeDwc3;"
+    "     'IOMatchCategory' = NativeDwc3;"
+    "     'IOProviderClass' = IOPlatformExpertDevice;"
+    "     'IOProbeScore'    = 400:32;"
+    "   }"
     ")";
